($t$Vigna angularis$t$, $t$Vigna angularis$t$, $t$Fabaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Fabaceae. Portamento: Annual. Altezza massima indicativa: 0.8 m. Vigna angularis, commonly known as Adzuki Bean or Red Mung Bean, is an annual vine in East Asia and the Himalayas. It grows usually about 30-90 cm in height. The root system is a taproot that can reach a depth of 40-50 cm. The leaves are trifoliate, pinnate, and arranged alternately along the stem on a long petiole. The flowers are bright yellow papilionaceous arranged in a cluster of 6-10. The fruits are smooth, cylindrical, and thin-walled pods. Adzuki bean is commonly sweetened before eating. It is eaten sprouted or boiled. It is also used in many Chinese dishes and as a filling in Japanese sweets. Tender young pods are cooked as a vegetable. Roasted seeds are used as a substitute for coffee. Medicinally, the beans are used in the treatment of kidney diseases, constipation, abscesses, certain tumors, threatened miscarriage, retained placenta, and non-secretion of milk. Seed sprouts are used to treat threatened abortion caused by injury. A flour made from the beans is used in making shampoos and facial creams. V. angularis is also grown as a green manure and for soil erosion control.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Adzuki Bean$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Fabaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consociazioni_favorevoli": [], "consociazioni_sfavorevoli": []}$j$::jsonb, $j${"adatta": null, "dimensione_minima_litri": null, "rinvaso_ogni_mesi": null, "irrigazione_fattore": null}$j$::jsonb, $t$annuale$t$, $t$vigna-angularis$t$, ARRAY[$t$Plants For A Future (pfaf.org) — importazione bozza automatica, dati non verificati manualmente$t$], $t$bozza$t$, null, null),
($t$Vigna hosei$t$, $t$Vigna hosei$t$, $t$Fabaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Fabaceae. Portamento: Perennial Climber. Altezza massima indicativa: 1 m. Sarawak Bean, Vigna hosei, is a perennial plant producing twining stems 1-2 m long that scrambles over the ground or twine into any surrounding vegetation. Although no plant part is edible and of medicinal important, the plant is an excellent ground cover and green manure crop. Seedling growth is vigorous and young plants quickly suppress growth of weed. It also has the ability to fix atmospheric nitrogen, hence it enriches the oil and promotes plant growth.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Abbondante, terreno costantemente umido", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Sarawak Bean$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Fabaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consociazioni_favorevoli": [], "consociazioni_sfavorevoli": []}$j$::jsonb, $j${"adatta": null, "dimensione_minima_litri": null, "rinvaso_ogni_mesi": null, "irrigazione_fattore": null}$j$::jsonb, $t$perenne$t$, $t$vigna-hosei$t$, ARRAY[$t$Plants For A Future (pfaf.org) — importazione bozza automatica, dati non verificati manualmente$t$], $t$bozza$t$, null, null),
($t$Vigna mungo$t$, $t$Vigna mungo$t$, $t$Fabaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Fabaceae. Portamento: Annual. Altezza massima indicativa: 1 m. Vigna mungo or also known in various common names such as Black Gram, Urd Bean, Black Matpe, and Black Mung Bean, is an erect, hairy, and bushy annual plant with a well-developed tap root and grows up to 100 cm in height. It is often grown in the Indian subcontinent. The pods are narrow and cylindrical with each pod containing about 4-10 small, black seeds. The leaves are composed of three oval leaflets each. Flowers are yellow and in dense clusters. Young seedpods and seeds are cooked and consumed as a vegetables. Dried seeds are boiled or ground into flour. The leaves are also edible. In traditional medicine, the seeds are used as a poultice on abscesses. Seed flour is rich in saponins and can be used as a substitute to soap. The plant has the ability to fix atmospheric nitrogen hence it is grown in some areas as green manure.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Abbondante, terreno costantemente umido", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Black Gram, Urd Bean, Black Matpe, Black Mung Bean$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Fabaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": nu